 interaction with key material for use in securing socket connections.\n2. **Input**: There are no direct parameters taken by this method; however, it relies on the internal state which should have been previously initialized with a key store and potentially a password.\n3. **Output**: Returns an array of key management interfaces, specifically designed for managing the keys stored in the initialized key store.\n4. **Procedure**: \n   - First, the method checks if the internal key store has been initialized. If not, it throws an exception indicating that the factory is not properly initialized.\n   - If the key store is initialized, the method creates and returns an array containing a single key manager initialized with the key store and the password (if provided).\n","group":"google/conscrypt","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"common/src/main/java/org/conscrypt/KeyManagerFactoryImpl.java","grade":2,"spans":[[113,119]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-cae9461a7ef607959711","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function is designed to create a certificate object from a provided input stream that contains the certificate data in a recognized format.\n2. **Input**: An input stream that should contain the certificate data, either in PEM or DER format.\n3. **Output**: Returns a certificate object if the parsing is successful. If the parsing fails due to data format issues, it throws an exception indicating the problem.\n4. **Procedure**: The function attempts to parse the certificate data from the input stream using a specific parser. If the parser encounters any issues (e.g., incorrect format, corrupted data), it catches a parsing exception and converts it into a certificate exception, which is then thrown to the caller.\n","group":"google/conscrypt","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"common/src/main/java/org/conscrypt/OpenSSLX509CertificateFactory.java","grade":2,"spans":[[296,303]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-e3808dd49d03029cad07","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: Decrypts a message that was previously encrypted using a corresponding encryption method, ensuring data confidentiality and integrity in secure communications.\n2. **Input**: A byte array representing the encrypted data and an optional byte array of associated data that can be used to provide additional contextual information for the decryption process.\n3. **Output**: A byte array containing the decrypted version of the input data, which is the original plaintext.\n4. **Procedure**: Utilizes the internal key schedule maintained by a cryptographic context specifically initialized for decryption. It checks if the context is properly initialized for decryption and not for encryption. If the initialization is correct, it proceeds to decrypt the encrypted data using the provided associated data if any. If decryption fails due to any issue such as incorrect keys or tampering, it throws a security exception.\n","group":"google/conscrypt","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"common/src/main/java/org/conscrypt/HpkeContextRecipient.java","grade":2,"spans":[[48,50]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-0b4e849011cefca33e89","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function is designed to release resources associated with a specific reference used in ASN.1 data reading operations, ensuring that system resources are properly managed and freed after use.\n2. **Input**: Accepts a long integer representing a reference to an ASN.1 data structure.\n3. **Output**: There is no return value as the primary function is to manage memory by freeing resources.\n4. **Procedure**: The function checks if the provided reference is non-zero and, if so, it releases any memory or resources tied to that reference. After execution, the reference should not be used in any subsequent operations to avoid errors or system crashes.\n","group":"google/conscrypt","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"common/src/main/java/org/conscrypt/NativeCrypto.java","grade":2,"spans":[[701,701]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-ccddf606e06a9bc504ae","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To retrieve the session context used for managing server-side SSL sessions.\n2. **Input**: None.\n3. **Output**: Returns an instance of the server session context.\n4. **Procedure**: The method directly returns the instance of the server session context that is maintained within the SSL context implementation.\n","group":"google/conscrypt","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"common/src/main/java/org/conscrypt/OpenSSLContextImpl.java","grade":2,"spans":[[149,152]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-9155c9f49743e505a39c","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function is designed to validate and set the encoded form of a cryptographic key based on the specified operation mode. It ensures that the key is suitable for encryption or decryption tasks.\n2. **Input**: The function takes two parameters: an integer representing the operation mode (such as encrypt or decrypt) and a cryptographic key object.\n3. **Output**: Returns the byte array representation of the cryptographic key if it passes all checks.\n4. **Procedure**: \n   - First, the function determines whether the operation is for encryption or decryption based on the operation mode.\n   - It then checks if the provided key is of the correct type (specifically, a secret key).\n   - The function retrieves and checks if the byte array representation of the key is non-null.\n   - It verifies that the size of the key is supported.\n   - Finally, it sets an internal representation of the key to its encoded form and returns this byte array.\n","group":"google/conscrypt","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"common/src/main/java/org/conscrypt/OpenSSLCipher.java","grade":2,"spans":[[461,481]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-6bcc22ffa28f732eae19","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To determine if the TLS Channel ID extension is active for a server socket, which is used for additional security measures in client-server communications.\n2. **Input**: None.\n3. **Output**: A boolean value indicating whether the extension is enabled (true) or not (false).\n4. **Procedure**: Simply returns the state of a private boolean field that represents whether the TLS Channel ID extension is enabled.\n","group":"google/conscrypt","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"common/src/main/java/org/conscrypt/ConscryptServerSocket.java","grade":2,"spans":[[129,131]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-e242f3ac495080286084","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To identify the enumeration type corresponding to a specified string that represents an encoding type for certificate paths.\n2. **Input**: A string representing the name of an encoding type.\n3. **Output**: The corresponding enumeration type if the input string matches one of the predefined encoding types; otherwise, `null`.\n4. **Procedure**: The function iterates through all values of the enumeration that defines encoding types. For each type, it checks if the input string matches the type's associated string identifier. If a match is found, that enumeration type is returned. If no match is found by the end of the iteration, the function returns `null`.\n","group":"google/conscrypt","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"common/src/main/java/org/conscrypt/OpenSSLX509CertPath.java","grade":2,"spans":[[61,69]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-7b2bc82f1346d07b6d38","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To evaluate the cryptographic strength and validity of a digital certificate by verifying its key length and signature algorithm against predefined security standards.\n2. **Input**: A single digital certificate of type X509Certificate.\n3. **Output**: Does not return any value; however, it throws a CertificateException if the certificate does not meet the required security criteria.\n4. **Procedure**: The function performs two main checks on the provided certificate: first, it verifies that the key length of the certificate's public key meets minimum security thresholds for RSA, DSA, and EC keys; second, it checks that the certificate's signature algorithm is not one of the deprecated or insecure algorithms listed in a predefined blacklist.\n","group":"google/conscrypt","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"common/src/main/java/org/conscrypt/ChainStrengthAnalyzer.java","grade":2,"spans":[[70,73]]}],"answerability":"answerable"}]}
